"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and a Phase 1 budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team has expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, including Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Key milestones include gathering R&D proposals by July 20th to enhance data visualization with AI, completing the design phase, and successfully finishing the testing phase, which is being celebrated on October 10th. The project is now moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November."
